From da52bb78c689241256399c29a03ae478df057936 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Beard <olib141@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Jan 2026 20:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] FROMLIST: lookandfeel/components: Split greeter logic
 from wallpaper fader; use underlay rather than shader

Splitting greeter logic out into a separate component allows usage in Plasma Login Manager, in which the wallpaper lives in a separate binary to the greeter.

Using an underlay rather than a the more complex shader makes things more maintainable, and brings us in-line with other aspects of the shell that want to adjust the wallpaper to create contrast, such as the Overview effect, which uses a blur with radius 64px and a background-coloured underlay to ensure good contrast.

Link: https://invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-workspace/-/merge_requests/6197
Signed-off-by: Mingcong Bai <jeffbai@aosc.io>
